1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,720
Minqin, lying in the city of Wuwei in Gansu, is sandwiched between China’s third- and fourth-largest deserts.
民勤位于甘肃省武威市，夹在中国第三大沙漠和第四大沙漠之间。

2
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:11,160
It is one of the country’s main sources of sandstorms.
这里是中国沙尘暴的主要发源地之一。

3
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:27,660
In 2007, then 26-year-old Ma Junhe started Minqin’s first environmental protection volunteer program named Save Minqin after reading in a newspaper that his hometown was at risk of being covered by sand within 17 years.
2007年，当时26岁的马俊河在报纸上读到家乡面临17年内被沙子覆盖的危险，之后便发起了民勤第一个环保志愿者项目，名叫“拯救民勤”。

4
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:31,040
The program started with just 60 volunteers.
这个项目刚开始时只有60名志愿者。

5
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:41,000
Last year, more than 6,000 volunteers planted suosuo trees there, most of whom were aged between 18 and 30, also called Gen Zers.
去年，6000多名志愿者在那里种下了梭梭树，其中大多数人年龄在18岁到30岁之间，也就是人们所说的Z世代。

6
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:48,100
Zhang Liwen, an 18-year-old girl from Xi’an, spent five days planting suosuo trees in Minqin.
来自西安的18岁女孩张丽雯花了五天时间在民勤种梭梭树。

7
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:56,890
“This idea came from my wish to complete a meaningful coming-of-age ceremony, but now I find value in contributing to society,” Zhang said.
张丽雯说：“这个想法源于我的心愿——完成一场有意义的成人礼，但现在我发现，为社会做贡献很有价值。”

8
00:00:57,690 --> 00:01:00,490
The vlogs shared by Zhang are lively and attractive.
张丽雯分享的视频日志生动活泼，很有吸引力。

9
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:12,120
She filmed a group of young volunteers, including herself, planting trees with stylish sports sunglasses, enjoying local noodles in their tent, and dancing in the desert after work.
她拍下了一群年轻志愿者（包括她自己）的身影：他们戴着时髦的运动太阳镜种树，在帐篷里享用当地面条，收工后在沙漠里跳舞。

10
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:18,170
Li Xiuniang, from Heilongjiang province, also posted her volunteer work online.
来自黑龙江省的李秀娘也在网上发布了自己的志愿服务经历。

11
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:22,570
“This task isn’t just for Minqin; it’s for all of China,” she said.
她说：“这项任务不只是为了民勤，更是为了整个中国。”

12
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:30,850
Lee Ting-Hsuan, a 20-year-old student from Taiwan, is one of thousands of volunteers who travel to Minqin every year.
来自台湾的20岁学生李亭萱是每年前往民勤的数千名志愿者之一。

13
00:01:31,650 --> 00:01:35,490
Around 20 young volunteers from Macao also joined the program.
来自澳门的约20名年轻志愿者也参加了这个项目。

14
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:42,220
“Through tree planting, we get a deeper understanding of Northwest China and its culture,” one of them said.
其中一人说：“通过植树，我们对中国西北地区及其文化有了更深入的了解。”

15
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:53,770
Since 2007, over 80,000 volunteers have joined this program and they have planted over 1.52 million trees, making a green promise in the yellow sands.
自2007年以来，已有8万多名志愿者参加了这个项目，种下了152万多棵树，在黄沙中许下了绿色的承诺。

16
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:58,810
Ma Junhe said, “Gen Zers are more confident in achieving their dreams.
马俊河说：“Z世代对实现自己的梦想更有信心。

17
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:07,290
They really enjoy meaningful public activities, and help a lot by sharing their stories online, attracting more people to take action.”
他们真的很喜欢有意义的公益活动，还通过在网上分享自己的故事帮了大忙，吸引更多人行动起来。”
